cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use BOAR in your research, please cite the SoftwareX article below."
title: "BOAR: Bayesian optimization for automated roughness calibration in two-dimensional hydrodynamic models"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/baw-de/BOAR"
url: "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.softx.2026.102899"
abstract: >-
  BOAR is an open-source Python framework for automated hydraulic roughness
  calibration in two-dimensional shallow-water numerical solvers. BOAR combines
  Bayesian optimization with conditional sampling to integrate expert knowledge,
  including feasible parameter ranges and inter-parameter constraints, thereby
  reducing the number of model evaluations.
keywords:
  - Bayesian optimization
  - Hydraulic roughness calibration
  - Shallow water solvers
  - BASEMENT
  - Surrogate model
  - Gaussian process
  - Model calibration
